WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
7 March 2023.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.040
Crowds march against the pension reform.

3
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.820
How many? «Selon le
ministère de l'Intérieur»:

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.090
1.28 million. «Selon la CGT»:

5
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.630
3.5 million. Even counting
the crowd is political.

6
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.010
The reform raised the
retirement age from 62 to 64.

7
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.840
In 2003, a prime minister had said:

8
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.970
«Ce n'est pas la rue qui
gouverne.» It still passed.

9
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.880
So who really holds power:

10
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.380
the street, or the ballot box?

11
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:35.080
In this mission, you'll weigh union
membership against what unions can do.

12
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.650
Then you'll plot protests
from 1936 to 2025:

13
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.100
did the government give way,

14
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.800
or not? Your mission: work out
who really holds power in France,

15
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.150
and back it with dates.
